Hi Tom,

About as.data.table I had to remind myself about auto-conversion.

data.table(df) drops through to as.data.table() anyway so doesn't do
auto-conversions of character to factor. There is some overhead checking
names and probably a copy is taken, so yes agree as.data.table is the
right one for setAs.

It seems it's just the 'data.table(letters[1:5],letters[6:10])' form that
does do auto-conversion of atomic character vectors to factor. Should we
remove the auto-conversion in that form then, for consistency? I think we
said setkey() would be the only place auto-conversion happens going
forward since that's where it's required.

Matthew


